{"texts": ["In honor of the 35th anniversary of the DEA, this spring\u2019s lecture series highlights Drug Kingpins \nAcross the Decades, with panel discussions covering Nicky Barnes & Frank Lucas (1970s), Pablo \nEscobar (1980s), The Arellano-Felix Organization (1990s) and Haji Baz Mohammad (2000s).\nDEA Museum Lecture Series\nDrug Kingpins Across the Decades\nRamon Arellano-Felix\nThe Arellano-Felix\nOrganization\nPlease join us for the third presentation in our Spring 2008 lecture series: \nMay 28, 2008, 10 A.M.\nDEA Museum Auditorium\nFor more information, please contact the DEA Museum Education Department at 202-307-3463\nPlease enter through the museum entrance on Hayes Street.\nThe Arellano-Felix Organization (AFO) was the most violent drug trafficking cartel in North \nAmerica. Based out of Tijuana, Mexico, AFO shipped tons of cocaine, heroin, and methamphet-\namine into the U.S. each year for over a decade. The organization was run by the Arellano-Felix \nfamily, which included brothers Benjamin, Ramon, Eduardo, Francisco Rafael and Francisco \nJavier. DEA Case Agents David Herrod and John Ziegler will present details of the case.\n* Sign Language Interpretation will be Provided *\nJavier Arellano-FelixEduardo Arellano-FelixBenjamin Arellano-Felix"], "vectors": [[-0.011806693859398365, -0.00531418202444911, -0.10230490565299988, -0.020978525280952454, 0.004718359559774399, 0.008534267544746399, -0.0338878333568573, 0.06581517308950424, -0.03059402108192444, -0.0033607380464673042, 0.016865186393260956, 0.07056250423192978, -0.003165577771142125, 0.053039949387311935, -0.014392618089914322, 0.016152774915099144, -0.0013523532543331385, 0.03536888584494591, 0.09373831748962402, -0.03806321322917938, 0.011385630816221237, -0.02212243154644966, 0.0060834698379039764, 0.014319602400064468, -0.08553440868854523, 0.09322336316108704, -0.06584316492080688, 0.03488006815314293, 0.016832325607538223, -0.011537805199623108, -0.06477324664592743, 0.1052631214261055, 0.